  "verificationScope": "Let K be a field and B a nonnegatively graded commutative K-algebra. For q > 0 use the exact original pieces B_(qn) in the original algebra S. The degree-zero chart rings are canonically isomorphic through equal fractions in the same original localization. For any homogeneous f,g and any x = fg, the comparison commutes with both chart restrictions as ring homomorphisms. The positive regraded denominators cover the original Proj because every positive homogeneous original denominator has the same basic open as its q-th power. The scheme gluing, original coefficient sheaf, fixed C_L and cut-dependent C_H identification, and same normalized geometric trace remain open. Original Lemmas 4.1 and 4.2 and the main theorem remain open. Whole local checkpoint 180.",
